ill to fight by whipping itself with its three tails, it charges at full speed.",[17]="Once it takes aim at its foe, it makes a headlong charge. It is famous for its violent nature.",[18]="Once it takes aim at its foe, it makes a headlong charge. It is famous for its violent nature.",[21]="Once it takes aim at its foe, it makes a headlong charge. It is famous for its violent nature.",[22]="Once it takes aim at its foe, it makes a headlong charge. It is famous for its violent nature.",[23]="After heightening its will to fight by whipping itself with its three tails, it charges at full speed.",[24]="When it is about to tackle, it whips its body repeatedly with its three long tails.",[25]="This Pokémon is not satisfied unless it is rampaging at all times. If there is no opponent for Tauros to battle, it will charge at thick trees and knock them down to calm itself.",[26]="This Pokémon is not satisfied unless it is rampaging at all times. If there is no opponent for Tauros to battle, it will charge at thick trees and knock them down to calm itself.",[27]="Historically, people in areas all over the world have ridden Tauros, but the practice is said to have started in Alola.",[28]="Although it’s known to be a fierce Pokémon, Tauros in the Alola region are said to possess a measure of calmness.",[29]="They live in groups. The one with the longest, thickest, and most-scarred horns is the boss of the herd.",[30]="The climate seems to be related to the reason Tauros in Alola are a little calmer than those in other regions.",[31]="A rowdy Pokémon with a lot of stamina. Once running, it won’t stop until it hits something.",[32]="A rowdy Pokémon with a lot of stamina. Once running, it won’t stop until it hits something.",[33]="When Tauros begins whipping itself with its tails, it’s a warning that the Pokémon is about to charge with astounding speed.",[34]="The Tauros of the Galar region are volatile in nature, and they won’t allow people to ride on their backs."},es={[23]="Después de animarse a luchar fustigándose con sus tres colas, carga a toda velocidad.",[24]="Cuando va a usar Placaje, se azota repetidas veces con las tres colas que tiene.",[25]="Este Pokémon no está contento a menos que esté continuamente de aquí para allá. Si no hay rival que luche contra Tauros, se estampa contra árboles grandes para calmarse y los embiste para echarlos abajo.",[26]="Este Pokémon no está contento a menos que esté continuamente de aquí para allá. Si no hay rival que luche contra Tauros, se estampa contra árboles grandes para calmarse y los embiste para echarlos abajo.",[27]="El uso de Tauros como montura se remonta a tiempos muy remotos. Ahora es una práctica muy extendida, pero parece que surgió en Alola.",[28]="Es un Pokémon muy famoso por su naturaleza violenta, aunque el Tauros de Alola parece ser algo más sosegado.",[29]="Vive en manadas dominadas por el ejemplar que luce la cornamenta más mellada y de mayor tamaño y grosor.",[30]="En Alola, los Tauros muestran un carácter más sosegado que en otras regiones. Posiblemente, esto guarde relación con lo apacible del clima.",[31]="Un Pokémon violento que rebosa energía. Cuando echa a correr, no se detiene hasta que choca con algo.",[32]="Un Pokémon violento que rebosa energía. Cuando echa a correr, no se detiene hasta que choca con algo.",[33]="Conviene tener cuidado si empieza a fustigarse con las colas, pues es señal de que va a cargar a máxima velocidad.",[34]="Los Tauros que habitan en la región de Galar son de temperamento irascible y no permiten que los humanos monten en su lomo."},pt="Os Tauros da região de Galar têm temperamento instável e não deixam que as pessoas montem em suas costas."},evo={{s=128}},moves={[1]={1,33,21,23,28,39,35,43,44,99,51,36},[2]={1,33,21,23,28,39,35,43,44,99,51,36},[3]={1,33,4,39,8,99,13,30,19,184,26,228,34,156,43,37,53,36},[4]={1,33,4,39,8,99,13,30,19,184,26,228,34,156,43,37,53,36},[5]={1,33,4,39,8,99,13,30,19,184,26,228,34,156,43,37,53,36},[6]={1,33,4,39,8,99,13,30